cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "RouteAgents: a measured playbook for post-route FPGA timing optimization (FPL'26 contest submission)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chatzitsompanis"
    given-names: "Georgios"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Geochatz3/routeagents-fpl26"
version: 5.5.3
date-released: "2026-08-10"
abstract: >-
  Submission to the FPL'26 Agentic FPGA Backend Optimization Contest,
  scoring 369.9 over 7 evaluation benchmarks with no validation failures.
  RouteAgents raises the Fmax of placed-and-routed Vivado designs under a
  wall-clock and LLM-cost budget using a library of 42 optimization plays,
  each carrying a measured trigger and a measured exclusion mined from an
  attributed run corpus. A router assigns a play class from measured design
  features alone; within that class a language model selects the operands.
  A control layer makes running them at full aggression affordable: a
  monotone validated bank, termination on an attested delay bound, and a
  stop rule derived algebraically from the scoring function.
keywords:
  - FPGA
  - timing optimization
  - LLM agents
  - Vivado
  - RapidWright
